# Arduino motor controller: a Keyestudio Uno R3-compatible board.
#
# Its USB-serial bridge is a Silicon Labs CP2102, 10c4:ea60 with the generic
# serial "0001" -- identical to the RPLIDAR's adapter, so the two can only be
# told apart by the USB port they are plugged into. See
# 99-heron-rplidar.rules for the full story; keep the two port assignments
# in step:
#
#   KERNELS "1-1.2"   the Arduino (this file)
#   KERNELS "1-1.4"   the LiDAR
#
# Code must open /dev/arduino, never /dev/ttyUSB*.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", KERNELS=="1-1.2", SYMLINK+="arduino", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"
